Z||000000||BN Boomer||01-12-2001||06:31 PM||||Well, they finally came and took away my first Fiero, an 87 coupe, the other day. Even if it was only a $300 car to start out with and probably wouldn't have been worth restoring, I feel bad that I wrecked her beyond repair and must now part with her. For some reason, I always get sentimental when getting rid of any vehicle, even if it was nothing but headaches for me. At least it's going to live on by donating it's remaining usable parts to other deserving Fieros....<P>Here she is being loaded up...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/boomers_fiero_files/mvc-004f.jpg"> <P>Looking a little tweaked...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/boomers_fiero_files/mvc-006f.jpg"> <P>And the fond farewell...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/boomers_fiero_files/mvc-007f.jpg"> ||||reg||9
Z||000001||Cheever2||01-12-2001||06:44 PM||||Everybody, alltogether...<BR>*Aaaawwww*<P>Isn't it customary to cover the deceased?  I really wouldn't want people to see a dead FIERO going down the road like that.  Give it some dignity.<BR> <BR>Sorry, got carried away.  I do have sympathy for you.  My regards.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 01-12-2001).]||||reg||6
