Z||000004||Bob Englert||01-12-2001||08:58 PM||||Lisa:<P>My black SE is going to it's new owner next week also.  He is driving over from AL with Ed and Rosey Parks to pick it up.  I will miss it since it was my first Fiero and runs excellent.  Just no room to keep it with 2 87 GT's in the garage.<P>At least it is going to a good home!<P><P>------------------<BR>Bob<BR>2 - 87 GT's<BR>85 SE 4 cyl||||reg||1
Z||000005||BN Boomer||01-12-2001||09:01 PM||||Lisa, <P>I only removed the fender to access the headlight control module between it and the firewall. If you look carefully, in the first pic you can see a reflection off the fender inside of the car. <P>Ogre,<P>What makes you think there are still headlights under the hood? Actually, there are. The ones off of my 85 GT, which I swapped with the ones from this car.<P>To both of you (and everyone else),<P>The car is being given to another local Fiero enthusiast. He paid for the tow truck. I don't believe he is very active on the Internet and to my knowledge isn't on this board, although I did tell him about it. This makes his 11th or 12th Fiero. I really wanted to avoid giving the car to a recycler/scrapper as I figured most of the parts would eventually just be crushed. I'm pleased that I was able to find someone who has the time and space to strip it.||||reg||6
